ividend of $0.27 per share. This dividend was paid on August 1, 2025.\n\nWe plan to use excess cash available at the Parent Company as efficiently as possible in the future. Excess cash flow, as we define it, results primarily from the dividends received by the Parent Company from its insurance subsidiaries less the interest paid on debt. The cash received by the Parent Company from our insurance subsidiaries is after they have made substantial investments during the year to grow the business. Possible uses of excess cash flow include, but are not limited to, share repurchases, acquisitions, shareholder dividend payments, investments in securities, or repayment of short-term debt. We will determine the best use of excess cash after ensuring that targeted capital levels are maintained in our insurance subsidiaries. If market conditions are favorable, we currently expect that share repurchases will continue to be a primary use of those funds.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPAYX Dividend History — All Payments, Growth Rate & Cuts | DivTrkr (https://www.divtrkr.com/dividends/PAYX/dividend-history)\nciteturn10search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; \n## How this growth is measured\n\nYear-over-year growth here compares each year's median payment with the year before, not the calendar-year total. Ex-dividend dates drift, so a quarterly payer can book five ex-dates in one calendar year and four in the next. Comparing raw yearly totals would show a phantom cut of around 25% in a year where the company did nothing but pay slightly earlier. Using the median payment removes that distortion, and also ignores one-off special dividends.\n\nYears marked “timing” booked a different number of payments than PAYX's usual cadence, so their total is not directly comparable with neighbouring years.\n\n## Recent PAYX dividend payments\n\nEx-dividend date  | Amount per share\n--- | ---\nJuly 28, 2026  | $1.19\nMay 13, 2026  | $1.19\nJanuary 28, 2026  | $1.08\nNovember 7, 2025  | $1.08\nJuly 21, 2025  | $1.08\nMay 12, 2025  | $1.08\nFebruary 7, 2025  | $0.980\nNovember 7, 2024  | $0.980\nAugust 8, 2024  | $0.980\nMay 9, 2024  | $0.980\nFebruary 12, 2024  | $0.890\nNovember 13, 2023  | $0.890\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPaychex Declares Quarterly Dividend (https://finance.yahoo.com/news/paychex-declares-quarterly-dividend-201500999.html)\nciteturn10search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.3 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; \n\n# Paychex Declares Quarterly Dividend\n\nBusiness Wire\n\nJuly 9, 2025 1 min read\n\n  * PAYX\n\n## Trading disclosure\n\nThe above button links to Coinbase. Yahoo Finance is not a broker-dealer or investment adviser and does not offer securities or cryptocurrencies for sale or facilitate trading. Coinbase pays us for certain activity generated through this link. Prices displayed are informational.\n\nLearn more\n\nImage\n\nROCHESTER, N.Y., July 09, 2025--(BUSINESS WIRE)--The Board of Directors of Paychex, Inc. (Nasdaq: PAYX) declared a regular quarterly cash dividend on Paychex common stock of $1.08 per share, payable on August 29, 2025, to shareholders of record as of July 21, 2025.\n\nAbout Paychex\nPaychex, Inc. (Nasdaq: PAYX) is the digitally driven HR leader that is reimagining how companies address the needs of today's workforce with the most comprehensive, flexible, and innovative HCM solutions for organizations of all sizes. Offering a full spectrum of HR advisory and employee solutions, Paychex pays one out of every 11 American private sector workers and is raising the bar in HCM for nearly 800,000 customers in the U.S. and Europe. Every member of the Paychex team is committed to fulfilling the Company's purpose of helping businesses succeed. Visit www.paychex.com to learn more.\n\nView source version on businesswire.com: https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250708006472/en/\n\nContacts\n\nInvestor Relations\nRachel White\nPaychex, Inc.\nHead of Investor Relations\n585-216-0822\ninvestors@paychex.com\nMedia Relations\nTracy Volkmann\nPaychex, Inc.\nManager, Public Relations\n585-387-6705\ntvolkmann@paychex.com--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGLOBE LIFE INC. DECLARES DIVIDEND | Nasdaq (https://www.nasdaq.com/press-release/globe-life-inc-declares-dividend-2025-04-24)\nciteturn10search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.5 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; \n\n# GLOBE LIFE INC. DECLARES DIVIDEND\n\n## \n\nPublished\n\nApr 24, 2025 4:15pm EDT\n\nMCKINNEY, Texas, April 24, 2025 /PRNewswire/ -- Globe Life Inc. (NYSE: GL) announced that its Board of Directors has declared a quarterly dividend of $.2700 per share on all of the outstanding common stock of the Company held of record as of close of business of the Company's transfer agent on July 3, 2025. The dividend will be paid on August 1, 2025.\n\nGlobe Life Inc. is a holding company specializing in life and supplemental health insurance for the middle-income market distributed through multiple channels, including direct to consumer and exclusive and independent agencies.\n\n \n\nImage: Cision View original content to download multimedia:https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/globe-life-inc-declares-dividend-302437556.html\n\nSOURCE Globe Life Inc.\n\nThe views and opinions expressed herein are the views and opinions of the author and do not necessarily reflect those of Nasdaq, Inc.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPaychex declares quarterly dividend of $1.08 per share By Investing.com (https://www.investing.com/news/company-news/paychex-declares-quarterly-dividend-of-108-per-share-93CH-4128889)\nciteturn10search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.3 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; \n\n# Paychex declares quarterly dividend of $1.08 per share\n\nPublished 07/09/2025, 04:21 PM\n\nImage: Paychex declares quarterly dividend of $1.08 per share\n\nPaychex declares quarterly dividend of $1.08 per share\n\nIn this article:\n\nPAYX-0.09%\n\nROCHESTER, N.Y. - Paychex, Inc. (NASDAQ:PAYX), a $52.6 billion market cap company with an impressive track record of 38 consecutive years of dividend payments, announced Wednesday that its Board of Directors has declared a regular quarterly cash dividend of $1.08 per share on the company’s common stock.\n\nThe dividend will be payable on August 29, 2025, to shareholders of record as of July 21, 2025, according to a press release statement from the HR services provider. The current dividend yield stands at 2.98%, reflecting the company’s 11-year streak of consecutive dividend increases, according to InvestingPro data.\n\nPaychex, which provides human capital management solutions, serves nearly 800,000 customers across the United States and Europe. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDoes Paychex (PAYX) Pay a Dividend? (2026) - Walnut AI Investing App (https://walnutinvest.com/stocks/payx/dividend)\nciteturn10search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; \nConsensus for the full fiscal year is ~$6.86B of revenue and ~$5.96 of EPS, and the next report is expected around December 18, 2026.\n\n## PAYX dividend at a glance\n\nDividend yield\n\n4.30%\n\nAnnual rate / share\n\n$4.76\n\nPayout ratio\n\n90.08%\n\nEx-dividend date\n\n2026-10-26\n\nRecent payments per share\n\n2026-07-28  | $1.19\n2026-05-13  | $1.19\n2026-01-28  | $1.08\n2025-11-07  | $1.08\n2025-07-21  | $1.08\n2025-05-12  | $1.08\n\nPAYX dividend data as of October 2026, sourced from Yahoo Finance and may be delayed. Yield moves with price and payout; confirm the current dividend and ex-date with PAYX's investor relations page before relying on it.\n\n## Is the PAYX dividend covered?\n\nPaychex paid out about 90% of its earnings as dividends, so the dividend absorbs nearly all earnings. There is little cushion at that level: if earnings fall, the company has to fund the payout from cash or debt, or cut it. Check the cash-flow coverage and the trend in earnings before treating the yield as dependable.\n\nCoverage is the question worth asking before yield. A dividend is only as good as the earnings behind it, and the highest yields on any screen are often the ones closest to being cut. Walnut is informational and is not an investment adviser.\n\n## How the PAYX dividend has changed\n\nThe latest payment of $1.19 per share compares with $1.08 in the equivalent payment a year earlier (July 21, 2025). That is a change of 10.2% over the year.\n\nA single year says little on its own. What dividend-growth investors track is the multi-year record: whether the payout has risen through a downturn, and whether the raises have kept pace with inflation. That record is on PAYX's investor relations page.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPaychex, Inc. Declares Quarterly Cash Dividend, Payable on August 29, 2025 | Finnhub (https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=793e535ca43ef6407f44cc529825e16d34ad3fd949b4d4a4c48a8c67d0c1f947)\nciteturn10search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.3 years ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; \n# Paychex, Inc. Declares Quarterly Cash Dividend, Payable on August 29, 2025\n\nPublished: 2025-07-09 17:05:23 ET PAYX\n\nPublished on 07/09/2025 at 17:05\n\nThe Board of Directors of Paychex, Inc. declared a regular quarterly cash dividend on Paychex common stock of $1.08 per share, payable on August 29, 2025, to shareholders of record as of July 21, 2025.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTECHNICAL DATA SHEET (https://resources.revvity.com/pdfs/6004051A.pdf)\nciteturn10search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; \nTECHNICAL DATA SHEET     \n     Reseach use only. Not for use in diagnostic procedures.\nCalibration Standards     \nCertificate of \nRadioactivity / Traceability\n3H Toluene Internal Standard\nProduct\nPart Number\n6004051A\n3